window.SEARCH_INDEX=[{"url": ".", "title": "Starwell Holdings", "text": "Dream with Starwell. A private holding company. We acquire and operate IT services companies in Israel, invest in real estate, and hold positions in public and private markets. ↓ What We Do Starwell IT Services Acquiring and operating IT Services businesses. Learn More → Starwell Real Estate Advisory mandates in Israel and limited partner investments in the United States. Learn More → Starwell Capital Long-term investment portfolio across public markets and direct private positions. Learn More → About Starwell Learn more about Starwell About Us →"}, {"url": "our-story", "title": "About Us", "text": "About Us Starwell Holdings Starwell is a private holding company that owns and operates businesses. It acquires and runs IT services companies, advises on, manages and invests in real estate, and allocates capital to public markets and alternative investments. As an owner-operator, Starwell takes an active role in what it controls: board seats, capital allocation, financing, shared infrastructure and hands-on support for management teams. Starwell Holdings was founded by Amit Kochavi, who serves as Chairman and CEO. Meet the team → Business Focus Our activities span three core areas: IT Services We build platforms in IT services - acquiring controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable companies and rolling them up into a larger group. We partner with owners and operators to preserve what works while adding the infrastructure and discipline of a platform built to last. Real Estate Advises on development projects in Israel, provides advisory and asset-management support to the family’s Tel Aviv portfolio, and invests as a limited partner in U.S. real estate. Capital Allocates across public equities and alternative investments to complement our operations. Strategy Our model is simple: operate where we have an edge, allocate where we don’t. Acquire and compound We prefer buying established, profitable businesses over starting from scratch - then compounding them, through operational improvement and further acquisitions. Proven cash flows, existing customer relationships, and experienced teams are the foundation; our job is to strengthen them, not replace them. Decentralized operations, centralized capital Portfolio companies run independently under their own management. What’s centralized is capital allocation: cash generated across the group is redeployed to its highest and best use, wherever that may be. Permanent ownership We have no fund cycles, no exit deadlines, and no pressure to sell. This lets us make decisions on a horizon measured in decades, hold through cycles, and be the buyer of choice for owners who care what happens to their business after the sale. Alignment over leverage We invest our own capital alongside partners and management, structure deals so that everyone wins together, and use debt conservatively - against proven cash flows, never against the balance sheet that anchors the group. Partnership We focus on selective, hig"}, {"url": "our-history", "title": "Our History", "text": "Our History Legacy Starwell builds on four generations of entrepreneurship, capital stewardship, and civic leadership - across Los Angeles, New York, and Tel Aviv. Max Factor The entrepreneurial root of the family traces to Max Factor , who built one of the defining consumer brands of the 20th century. From a single Los Angeles shop, he transformed the global cosmetics industry through invention, craftsmanship, and an uncompromising standard of quality - proof that enduring businesses are built product by product, customer by customer. Max Factor Max Factor David M. Heyman David M. Heyman David M. Heyman The tradition of disciplined capital stewardship runs through David M. Heyman , a New York financier and philanthropist who led the New York Foundation for decades. He treated capital as an instrument of long-term responsibility - to institutions, to communities, and to the generations that follow. Real assets, two cities The family’s real estate roots run in parallel on both sides of the ocean. In Los Angeles, Herb Glaser - attorney turned developer - built Glaser Development Company into a commercial real estate developer across Southern California and the Western United States, spanning logistics centers, warehouses, and multifamily properties, alongside decades of leadership in the city’s civic and Jewish institutions. In Tel Aviv, the Buchman family built a textile enterprise and converted it into real estate holdings that grew with the city itself. That tradition continues today through Doron Kochavi , attorney and real estate developer. Doron Kochavi Starwell Starwell is the modern expression of these roots: a private holding company that acquires and builds operating businesses, develops real assets, and allocates capital for the long term. The underlying values are inherited, not invented - integrity, patient ownership, and the responsibility to build things that endure."}, {"url": "our-team", "title": "Our Team", "text": "Our Team Leadership Starwell Holdings Amit Kochavi Chairman, CEO & Founder Amit founded Starwell Holdings to build a private investment and operating company that combines long-term capital with operational execution. He served in the Israeli Air Force’s Ofek technology unit. In 2019 he founded Circles I.T. Innovation Ltd., which merged its operations with Doss in 2025. He was named to Forbes Israel 30 Under 30 in 2017 and to TheMarker 40 Under 40 in 2025. He is Senior Advisor to the Mayor of Sderot, a member of the President of Israel’s Kol HaAm Council, and a member of the Board of Governors of Sapir Academic College. Amit continues to grow Starwell’s portfolio of platforms and partnerships, focused on building enduring value across cycles and geographies. LinkedIn X Shirly Gur Arie Executive Assistant Shirly supports Starwell’s leadership and day-to-day operations, coordinating across the firm’s platforms and partners to keep the organization running smoothly. LinkedIn Starwell IT Services Tal Raif Partner and Board Member, Starwell IT Services Tal is Amit’s partner in Starwell IT Services and sits on its board. Tal is Head of Strategy, Innovation and M&A at Afcon Holdings (TASE: AFHL), where he leads M&A end to end, from sourcing and valuation through due diligence and negotiation, alongside corporate venture investments and strategic partnerships across renewable energy, EV charging infrastructure, data centers, industrial automation, and defense technology. He is a third-generation member of the family behind Shlomo Group, and takes part in its strategic and investment activity across mobility, insurance and finance, real estate, shipyards, and aviation. He represents the family in international family-office forums, including The Family Office Alliance. He sits on the investment committee of Square One Labs and reviews opportunities across venture capital and private equity. He holds an MBA from the Coller School of Management at Tel Aviv University and a BA in Communication and Media Studies from IDC Herzliya. LinkedIn"}, {"url": "it-services", "title": "Starwell IT Services", "text": "Starwell IT Services Acquiring controlling or significant stakes in IT services companies, in Israel and beyond. The Thesis The IT services market is large, growing, and highly fragmented. Most of it consists of independent companies built on expertise and long-standing client relationships, without the backing of a larger group. In a technology landscape that never stops changing - cloud migration, artificial intelligence, and successive waves of transformation - businesses need a trusted external technology partner more than ever. Starwell IT Services acquires controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable IT services companies. We partner with owners and operators to preserve what works, while building around them the infrastructure and discipline of a platform built to last. 01 Acquire Controlling or significant stakes in established, profitable IT services companies. 02 Integrate Central systems, shared infrastructure, and a consistent standard of service across the portfolio. 03 Grow Operational improvement, talent development, and expanded service capabilities, driving long-term value creation. Acquisition criteria Established and profitable Israeli IT services companies with a history of profitable operation. Scale Annual revenue in the tens of millions of shekels, with teams of dozens of employees. Stake Controlling or significant stakes. Continuity We keep management, employees, and client relationships in place. Owners considering a sale are welcome to contact us in full confidence. Contact us → What owners can expect Permanent ownership We buy to hold. The companies we acquire are not packaged for resale. No fund clock We have no fund cycles and no exit deadlines, so there is no pressure to sell. A fast and discreet process A small team, direct conversations, and confidentiality at every stage. Team Amit Kochavi Executive Chairman Amit is the founder, chairman and CEO of Starwell Holdings. He founded Circles I.T. Innovation Ltd. in 2019, which merged its operations with Doss in 2025, and leads Starwell’s acquisition of IT services companies in Israel. Full biography → LinkedIn Tal Raif Partner and Board Member, Starwell IT Services Tal is Amit’s partner in Starwell IT Services and sits on its board. Tal is Head of Strategy, Innovation and M&A at Afcon Holdings (TASE: AFHL), where he leads M&A end to end, from sourcing and valuation "}, {"url": "real-estate", "title": "Starwell Real Estate", "text": "Starwell Real Estate Advisory mandates in Israel and limited partner investments in the United States. Markets Israel Advisory Advisory mandates on residential and mixed-use projects in Tel Aviv and central Israel, working alongside the institutional developers and public-sector partners who run them. Focus on urban renewal and projects with structural demand tailwinds. United States Capital Allocation Limited partner investments in value-add multifamily and industrial logistics strategies, alongside institutional operators with demonstrated track records. Starwell Positions held by Starwell: advisory mandates, participation in development projects alongside the developers who run them, and limited partner investments. Urban Renewal Rova 7 - Mevoot Yafo ● Tel Aviv, Israel ■ Strategic Advisory - municipality relations, commercial concept, and marketing strategy △ Keren Reality, Kardan Real Estate (50/50 JV) 55-dunam urban renewal project encompassing approximately 890 residential units, 5,000 sqm of commercial space, 20,000 sqm of office space, and 12 dunams of public area. Approved master plan (May 2023). Multifamily The Dawson ● Cartersville, Georgia, US ■ Limited Partner △ Wilpon & Co. 192-unit multifamily value-add acquisition. Industrial Logistics Terminal Logistics Fund II ● US Logistics Markets ■ Limited Partner △ Center Capital Partners Private real estate fund focused on industrial logistics assets across US markets. Website → Family track record Doron Kochavi has developed or co-developed the projects below, totaling more than 1,250 residential units. They are shown as family background and are not Starwell holdings. Beyond Towers, Tel Aviv ■ Advisory and owner representative (Doron Kochavi) △ Tidhar Group, Union Group, Himnuta-KKL Large-scale mixed-use development comprising office, residential, and commercial space. Total project value estimated at NIS 4 to 4.5 billion. Vitkin 20, Tel Aviv ■ Residential Yedidya Frenkel 2, Tel Aviv ■ Residential and retail Marc Chagall 8, Tel Aviv ■ Residential Yehezkel Streichman 5-7, Tel Aviv ■ Residential and retail Arthur Rubinstein 10, Tel Aviv ■ Completed and leased Einstein 1-5, Tel Aviv ■ With Hagag Group. Under construction Hi Tower, Givatayim ■ Residential"}, {"url": "capital", "title": "Starwell Capital", "text": "Starwell Capital Long-term investment portfolio across public markets and direct private positions. Approach Patient, long-term capital allocation across public markets and direct private positions. Starwell Capital holds the group’s investment portfolio outside the operating companies. The mandate spans long-term public market holdings and direct private positions. We invest with a long time horizon and concentrate where we have genuine conviction. Starwell invests only its own capital and does not manage third-party funds or solicit investments. 01 Public Markets A diversified long-term core in low-cost global index funds. 02 Direct Private Positions Private equity investments in buy-out and roll-up strategies, acquiring and improving traditional businesses through operational, financial, and technological efficiency. Portfolio Pioneers (Legion Holdings) Role: Investor An AI-native roll-up of healthcare staffing agencies. Website → Kodiak Fund I Role: Investor A long-term partner for aspiring small business owners, backing the next generation of American owner-operators with equity financing and support across due diligence, transaction structuring, capital raising, and ongoing operations. Website →"}, {"url": "news", "title": "News", "text": "News News & Insights Company news, market commentary, and updates on our investments. Latest All Company News Real Estate Company News Company News 2026 Amit Kochavi joins the Board of Governors of Sapir Academic College Amit Kochavi has joined the Board of Governors of Sapir Academic College, alongside his role as Senior Advisor to the Mayor of Sderot. Read More → Company News Company News Jun 3, 2025 Circles Merges Operations with U.S.-Based Doss Circles is merging its operations with U.S.-based Doss and will become the Israeli sales and marketing center for the company. Read More → Real Estate Real Estate May 6, 2025 Lee & Associates Atlanta Facilitates Sale of 28-Acre Industrial Site to Terminal Logistics Center Capital's IOS platform, Terminal Logistics, has acquired a 28-acre site in Gainesville, GA. Read More → Company News Company News Jan 1, 2025 Amit Kochavi named to TheMarker 40 Under 40 Amit Kochavi, founder and CEO of Starwell Holdings, appears on TheMarker&rsquo;s 40 Under 40 list for 2025. Read More →"}, {"url": "contact", "title": "Contact", "text": "Contact Get in Touch For inquiries about investment opportunities, partnerships, or potential transactions, please complete the form below. A member of our team will respond promptly. Leave empty: First Name * Last Name * Organization Email * Subject Message Submit Offices Givatayim Beyond Towers Ariel Sharon Street 1 Givatayim, Israel Los Angeles 11601 Wilshire Blvd #2080 Los Angeles, CA 90025 USA"}, {"url": "careers", "title": "Careers", "text": "Join Us Careers at Starwell We’re a small, high-conviction team building platforms across IT Services and Real Estate, with passive capital allocation to public markets and alternative assets. We look for people who think long-term and operate with precision. How We Work Long-Term Thinking We build for decades, not quarters. Every decision is made with durability and permanence in mind. Operational Excellence We get into the details. Great outcomes come from rigorous execution and deep domain knowledge. Integrity We say what we mean and do what we say - with partners, portfolio companies, and each other. Entrepreneurial Spirit We are builders. We back people who create things that didn’t exist before. Working with us We do not run a standing job board. We hire when we meet the right person, so we read everything that reaches us. Send a CV and a short note about the work you want to do to shirly@starwellholdings.com . Get in Touch"}, {"url": "privacy", "title": "Privacy Policy", "text": "Legal Privacy Policy Draft. This policy is pending legal review and is not yet in force. Who we are Starwell Holdings Ltd., Company No. 517166237. Registered address: [details from counsel]. What we collect If you write to us through the contact form we receive the first and last name, organization, email address, subject and message you enter. We do not ask for any other personal detail, and the site does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Why we hold it To read your message and reply to it. Legal basis: [details from counsel]. Who processes it Form submissions are handled by our hosting provider’s form service and reach us by email. Further processors, and any transfer of data outside Israel: [details from counsel]. How long we keep it [details from counsel] Your rights Rights of access, correction and deletion, and the procedure for exercising them: [details from counsel]. Contact Questions about this policy: amit@starwellholdings.com . Last updated: [details from counsel]."}, {"url": "accessibility", "title": "Accessibility Statement", "text": "Legal Accessibility Statement Draft. This statement is pending legal review and is not yet in force. Our commitment Starwell Holdings Ltd. works to keep this website usable by as many people as possible, including people using assistive technology. Standard Standard applied and level of conformance: [details from counsel]. What has been done The site is built with semantic HTML and landmark regions, can be operated by keyboard, keeps text and background contrast high in both the light and dark colour schemes, labels every image and form field, respects the operating system’s reduced-motion setting, and reflows to a single column on small screens without horizontal scrolling. Known limitations [details from counsel] Accessibility coordinator Name, telephone and email: [details from counsel]. Reporting a problem If you run into an accessibility problem on this site, please write to amit@starwellholdings.com and tell us the page and what happened. Date of this statement: [details from counsel]."}, {"url": "sitemap", "title": "Sitemap", "text": "Sitemap Sitemap Every page on the Starwell Holdings website, organized in one place. Company Home About Us Our Team Our History News Careers What We Do IT Services Real Estate Capital Resources Contact Search Sitemap עברית"}];
